"""Explicit source-checked Ramakrishna Neevel/Hatcher group decisions."""
import json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
LEDGER={x['claim_id']:x for x in map(json.loads,(ROOT/'decision-ledger.jsonl').open())}
GROUP=next(g for g in json.loads((ROOT/'source-review-groups.json').read_text())['groups'] if 'walter g neevel' in g['work_key'])

SOURCES={
 'NH':('d5a13923-a194-487e-8a9b-0d61f574d7e7','https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/philosophy-and-religion/hinduism-biographies/ramakrishna','Walter G. Neevel Jr. and Brian A. Hatcher, Encyclopedia of Religion entry (1987; revised 2005); first entry only, lines 29–99'),
 'ORDER':(None,'https://belurmath.org/sri-ramakrishna/','Ramakrishna Math and Ramakrishna Mission, official Sri Ramakrishna biography; community account'),
 'MULLER':(None,'https://tianmu.org/good-work-library/hindu/general-texts/ramakrishna-his-life-and-sayings-f-max-mller','F. Max Müller, Ramakrishna: His Life and Sayings (1898), digitized text of original book; title and text cross-checked against book metadata'),
 'KRIPAL':(None,'https://www.ruf.rice.edu/~kalischi/textuality.html','Jeffrey J. Kripal, author’s explanation of Kali’s Child and its interpretive claims; primary statement by scholar'),
 'SARADANANDA':(None,'https://www.ramakrishnavivekananda.info/sriramakrishna_thegreatmaster/2_14_madhura_sadhana.htm','Swami Saradananda, Sri Ramakrishna: The Great Master, chapter 2.14; Ramakrishna Order account'),
}

# prefix, decision, wording (None means original), epistemic type, [(source, locator)], rationale, limitation
REVIEWS=[
 ('1d1cf9df','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Teachings, lines 59–64')],'The entry explicitly contrasts formless-absolute reduction with experience of divine power in forms and gives the yato mat saying.','This verifies Neevel/Hatcher’s reading, not an exclusive interpretation shared by all scholars.'),
 ('3700d177','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Interpretations, lines 67–70')],'Hatcher expressly describes Neevel’s 1976 argument building on Zimmer and its Tantric-nondual interpretation.','The claim attributes Neevel’s position; it does not decide the disputed classification.'),
 ('3ee6fdc4','REVISE AND APPROVE','Hatcher argues that late-Victorian stigma around Tantra made early disciples wary of emphasizing it, and that prudery among devotees and Western interpreters contributed to some aspects of Ramakrishna’s psychosexual life being denied or explained away.','SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Interpretations, lines 74–77')],'The passage presents a scholarly explanation and uses cautious language. The revision names Hatcher and avoids asserting historical motives as settled fact.','This is Hatcher’s contested interpretation of reception history, not direct evidence of each disciple’s motive.'),
 ('4fe46d59','APPROVE',None,'TEXTUAL_HISTORY',[('NH','Teachings, line 58'),('ORDER','The Gospel of Sri Ramakrishna, lines 163–165')],'Independent scholarly and Order descriptions agree that Gupta recorded the conversations and Nikhilananda translated the Gospel.','The publication history is summarized; exact dates of all Kathamrita volumes are not asserted.'),
 ('56d372f8','REVISE AND APPROVE','Jeffrey Kripal offered a contested psychoanalytic reading of Ramakrishna involving homoerotic themes and possible sexual trauma. Hatcher’s scholarly account says Kripal rejected reducing Ramakrishna’s spirituality to pathology. These are interpretations, not established biographical facts.','CONTESTED_SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('KRIPAL','Author’s response, lines 54–60, 72–74'),('NH','Interpretations, lines 78–82')],'Kripal’s own explanation documents his sexual-trauma thesis; Hatcher documents his non-reductive claim. The original wording could be mistaken for factual allegations.','Highly contested sensitive interpretation; no independent historical finding of abuse or sexual orientation is asserted.'),
 ('5aea2401','REVISE AND APPROVE','In the preface to his 1898 book Ramakrishna: His Life and Sayings, Max Müller says he asked Vivekananda for an account of his teacher and received one; the Encyclopedia of Religion lists the work as an early Western account.','HISTORICAL_DOCUMENTATION',[('MULLER','Title/date, lines 13–19; book text, line 239'),('NH','Bibliography, line 89')],'Müller’s own text directly confirms his request and the received account. The encyclopedia bibliography gives 1899, apparently a later edition; original 1898 title metadata resolves the date.','The encyclopedia bibliography cites an 1899 edition; wording specifies the 1898 book text.'),
 ('709e10d2','REVISE AND APPROVE','In a letter quoted by Max Müller, Protap Chunder Mozoomdar disputed describing Ramakrishna as a Vedantist except in a broad cultural sense. Neevel and Hatcher contrast the Order’s Advaita-centered account with scholarly debate over the importance of Tantra and Vedanta.','CONTESTED_SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('MULLER','Mozoomdar letter quoted in Müller, lines 419–424'),('NH','Life, lines 45–46; Interpretations, lines 67–74')],'Müller directly prints Mozoomdar’s contrasting view. Hatcher documents the official/scholarly interpretive divide. The revision avoids implying one view wins.','The letter is known here through Müller’s reproduction, not the surviving manuscript; the precise quoted phrase is not repeated in corpus wording.'),
 ('70c1dffa','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Life, lines 49–50')],'The entry explicitly explains the appeal to educated visitors in colonial Calcutta in these terms.','This is Hatcher’s historical interpretation of visitors’ responses.'),
 ('996d54e9','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_ATTRIBUTION',[('NH','Life, lines 47–48')],'The entry directly reports the three- and four-day practices, visions, and conclusion. The claim attributes the account to a scholarly reference work.','Specific visionary experiences remain reported experiences, not independently verifiable events.'),
 ('a34c7f26','APPROVE',None,'CONTESTED_SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Interpretations, lines 70–73'),('ORDER','Message, lines 182–184')],'Hatcher states the continuity question and Kathamrita evidence; the Order articulates service to God in people.','The two source traditions differ; the corpus wording keeps the debate explicit.'),
 ('a46df63b','REVISE AND APPROVE','Neevel and Hatcher describe Vivekananda’s Practical Vedanta as a creative contribution to the movement and report scholarly theories connecting it to Western morality and Western reconstructions of Vedanta.','SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Life, line 53; Interpretations, lines 71–73')],'The entry supports creative contribution and alternate Western influences. The original’s Brahmo-influence clause is not established in this passage.','These are reported scholarly theories, not a settled causal account.'),
 ('b43a959b','REVISE AND APPROVE','The Order’s biography and Neevel–Hatcher’s scholarly entry both describe Ramakrishna’s practice of multiple paths, including Kali devotion, Tantra, Vaishnava practice, Advaita, Islam, and Christianity, as experiential disciplines.','SYNTHETIC_SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Life, lines 37–48'),('ORDER','Intense Spiritual Practices and Following Other Faiths, lines 147–153')],'Both inspected accounts support the breadth and practice-based sequence. The claim’s images-of-Mahavira-and-Christ detail is not supported by these passages and is omitted.','The accounts report religious practice and visions; they do not independently validate supernatural realization.'),
 ('c8d59d4f','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Life, lines 52–55')],'The entry explicitly notes Sarada’s posthumous status and interprets it using both service and Divine Mother themes.','Interpretive account of religious status and its symbolism.'),
 ('d4303758','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Life, lines 41–44')],'The entry describes Yogeshvari’s Tantric guidance and Hatcher’s interpretation of its effect on Ramakrishna’s theology.','The psychological transformation is a scholarly reading of religious biographical reports.'),
 ('d8394e89','APPROVE',None,'SCHOLARLY_INTERPRETATION',[('NH','Teachings/Interpretations, lines 59–60, 67–74')],'The entry directly contrasts official Advaita primacy with Tantric interpretations and asks why Tantra was downplayed.','The statement reports a scholarly characterization of the Order, which the Order may contest.'),
 ('e25fbaa7','REVISE AND APPROVE','The Neevel–Hatcher Encyclopedia of Religion entry gives Ramakrishna’s dates as 1834/6–1886 and identifies his birth name as Gadadhar Chatterjee and family as Vaishnava Brahmin; Belur Math gives 18 February 1836 as his birth date.','SOURCE_DISAGREEMENT',[('NH','Lead and Life, lines 29–35'),('ORDER','Sri Ramakrishna, lines 140–143, 166–168')],'Two inspected sources use different precision for the birth date while agreeing on 1886 death. The revision changes “reference works” to this specific entry.','The entry’s 1834/6 notation preserves uncertainty; the Order’s exact birth date is traditional institutional chronology.'),
 ('ee73dc34','REVISE AND APPROVE','Saradananda’s Order biography says Ramakrishna adopted women’s dress and ornaments during madhura-bhava practice associated with the women of Vraja, and that Mathur supplied the attire. Neevel–Hatcher note that this aspect of his life was often played down in later accounts.','TRADITIONAL_ACCOUNT_AND_SCHOLARLY_RECEPTION',[('SARADANANDA','The Master’s Sadhana of the Madhura Bhava, sections 5–9, lines 23–43'),('NH','Interpretations, lines 75–77')],'The Order account directly reports attire and devotional identification; the scholarly entry supplies reception context. Wording identifies each source’s perspective.','Saradananda reports a devotional account; later interpretation of why it was downplayed remains contested.'),
]

def cid(prefix):
    hits=[i for i in GROUP['pending_claim_ids'] if i.startswith(prefix)]
    assert len(hits)==1,(prefix,hits)
    return hits[0]

out=[]
for prefix,decision,wording,kind,refs,rationale,limitation in REVIEWS:
    i=cid(prefix);c=LEDGER[i];assert c['decision'] is None
    evidence=[]
    for key,loc in refs:
        sid,url,authority=SOURCES[key]
        evidence.append({'source_id':sid,'url':url,'locator':loc,'source_authority':authority,'independence_assessment':'Distinct scholarly and institutional works where multiple works are listed; shared tradition and possible source dependence are not counted as independent historical corroboration.','original_source_inspected':True,'original_claim_source_linked':sid in c['original_source_ids'] if sid else False})
    out.append({'claim_id':i,'personality':'Ramakrishna Paramahamsa','original_claim_text':c['original_claim_text'],'decision':decision,'final_proposed_wording':wording or c['original_claim_text'],'epistemic_type':kind,'evidence_references':evidence,'verification_rationale':rationale,'original_source_inspected':True,'material_limitation':limitation,'removal_reason':None})
assert len(out)==17 and len({x['claim_id'] for x in out})==17
(ROOT/'worker-ramakrishna-neevel-decisions.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(len(out),sum(d['decision']=='APPROVE' for d in out),sum(d['decision']=='REVISE AND APPROVE' for d in out))
